592186475899 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475899 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475505 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475899 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475540 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475899 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475899 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475899 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475899 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475899 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186475540 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475899 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e1839f04-52db-5ce7-ac3e-01d49177c51f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475906 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475454 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475906 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475906 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475906 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475733 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475906 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475906 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475906 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475906 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186475454 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475906 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fadcac08-89d6-5545-838e-e0a8639a57f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475909 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186475899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475909 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82211" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475909 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475909 #edb/ref 1071 "Change the order of integration in the double integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2y+1}^{3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475909 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "00b86b57-002e-5667-8521-28c6ba4d5298" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475909 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/03/03a006f46e78ec893c21d2a871c54eeccbdb0d74b19385a6a569f787ee1bdd2d.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,2y+1\\le x\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=2y+1\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{x-1}{2},\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{x-1}{2}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/d2/d27e38c7c3de8dda353151cd0347d6bead91cb19d2eb90d08dd485d77899bc27.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2y+1}^{3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{(x-1)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475914 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186475906 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475914 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82264" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475914 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475914 #edb/ref 1071 "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}-1}^{1-{x}^{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475914 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0e844cdc-bfeb-5b03-bf45-d36a53583297" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475914 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/37/374acdaf337d1977f938fc66a19a8b933a4464f922c7e9fd45fd39a6cacf920e.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}-1\\le y\\le 1-{x}^{3}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type II regions. \n\n![](images/cf/cf06c4d0e0189b8b3e3c60af788c0aa082755db9b9fab17ed0562e79e11cabe9.png)\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the lower region, written in the form $x=x(y),$  is \n\n$\\,$ $x=\\sqrt{y+1}.$\n\nAlso, the right boundary of the upper region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$\\,$ $x=\\sqrt[3]{1-y}.$\n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y+1}\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{1-y}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}-1}^{1-{x}^{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475929 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186475896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475929 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82342" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475929 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475929 #edb/ref 1071 "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475929 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2f7d21f4-2434-59d0-b158-63a98b31b96d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475929 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/69/69bff6ba843a7d93cc9c60ec0adfe5986d4eea78beeca8806ec487c64f32310a.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-x\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\nx=1\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=4-x\\,⟹\\,x=4-y.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,1\\le x\\le 4-y\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/47/47bc45edcaaa73ec6fb6010aa6d6fe35c77219b234d7f2b7210f12cec55e500d.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475945 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186475834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475945 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82209" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475945 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475945 #edb/ref 1071 "Change the order of integration in the double integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475945 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8d54021f-0d37-540b-875f-4f433fa4e2b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475945 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/48/48a1ef0d61b8b81e2fa0649b95a329099d48a802a5339d730f2da9cf8b59f547.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,1\\le x\\le 2-{y}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=2-{y}^{2}\\,⟹\\,y=\\sqrt{2-x},\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{2-x}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/22/22d41ecc443e1520035f52fefe524d88062432ab1643aa19b2e0b76185b191a0.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475966 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186475846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475966 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132646" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475966 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475966 #edb/ref 1071 "${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\int }_{{e}^{y}}^{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475966 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cb97248a-192c-5cf9-ad2e-d068b8748779" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475966 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/7e/7e0a0b1860f316f7954e85b9d7f6567d9e0c05bf316cb8af3901037abe6fd17e.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡5,\\,{e}^{y}\\le x\\le 5\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx={e}^{y}\\,⟹\\,y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 5,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/3c/3c95dd90ad02ab708f5893e47e7d7d0c8a212c18aed1972fb1bba1362181c383.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{\\int }_{{e}^{y}}^{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x)[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x)\\cdot y\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-x)\\,{|}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-5)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475971 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186475835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475971 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82252" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475971 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475971 #edb/ref 1071 "By changing the order of integration in the following double integrals, express the following sum as a single double integral.\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475971 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d9c15809-274b-5c74-bd5b-6fd325ecdfd9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475971 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/20/20055a4c35ca0fdcb119e69118861d9139d23f404ecb530cf7c1b9ecf39a96d6.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It consists of two type I regions, given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}\\}\\,\\cup \\,\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{2-x}\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{x}\\,⟹\\,x={y}^{2}\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{2-x}\\,⟹\\,x=2-{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le 2-{y}^{2}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/77/77dda47f9036b7019f0d2ea5d72c1b81e5778e5d7108760a3b0394a213690304.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{2-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475974 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186475848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475974 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82353" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475974 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475974 #edb/ref 1071 "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x/2}^{1/2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475974 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e49d891d-abb2-5ea6-ab4c-68e975346cd4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186475974 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/b6/b6b672e4776973f14b8ecff1fc35bcdd50c4229ade12ec74dc09c5327223c25f.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\frac{x}{2}\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x)$ is\n\n$$\nx=0,\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{2}\\,⟹\\,x=2y.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as type II region. Its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,0\\le x\\le 2y\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/09/09f6f71eaf66fe10e73b80ae59a30ddd04478de71dbe37c749674ac9f10d5bd4.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x/2}^{1/2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})[{\\int }_{0}^{2y}\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})[x]_{0}^{2y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}2y\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})]_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
